  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VAtr">V Atr</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-g">⁊ ures hlafordes gerædnes ⁊ his witena is, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man Cristene men for ealles to lytlu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> to deaðe ne fordeme.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-g2">⁊ witena gerædnes is, þæt man Cristene mæn for ealles to lytlum to deaðe ne fordeme.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="3[a]" corresp="#wit-d">⁊ ures hlafordes gerædnes ⁊ his witena is, þæt man Cristene men for ealles to litlum to deaðe ne fordeme;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And it is the decree of our lord and his councillors, that Christian men shall not be condemned to death for too trivial offences,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Verordnung unseres Herrn und seiner Witan ist, dass man christliche Menschen nicht für gar zu Geringes zum Tode verurtheile.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And it is the ordinance of our lord and his witan that Christian people are not to be condemned to death for all too small [offences].</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Af El. 49.7.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
